                <pb facs="0320" n="312" xml:id="pg312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.77/59: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-16T18:00:00+03:00">August 16, 1941—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 17—7:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1164. My 737, July [<hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>] 16, 4 p.m. for Feis.
                    Delighted to learn of orders placed for rolling stock for Egypt. Be sure not to
                    forget necessity for sending transportation experts and the sooner the better.
                    Greetings.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
